Carafe: every Wine thread carries a stop request the server can set.
The registry entry of a thread gets two words, a request (1 suspend, 2 end) and an exit code, and the thread
keeps a pointer to them. wine_nx_thread_stop_request sets or clears a request by TEB and thread id, wakes the
thread if it sleeps on its request (wine_nx_stop_sleep) and gives the thread's kernel handle;
wine_nx_in_runtime_code tells whether an address is the runtime's own code.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

